     fflloowwccttll — ng_netflow(4) control utility

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     fflloowwccttll [--dd _l_e_v_e_l] _p_a_t_h _c_o_m_m_a_n_d

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The fflloowwccttll utility is intended to control the ng_netflow(4) nodes.  It
     has a single option:

     --dd _l_e_v_e_l  Set the netgraph(3) debugging level to _l_e_v_e_l.

CCOOMMMMAANNDDSS
     Currently, fflloowwccttll supports only one command.

     sshhooww [iippvv44||iippvv66] [hhuummaann||vveerrbboossee]
           This command is the analog of the “show ip cache flow” command of a
           Cisco router.  It dumps the contents of the flow cache in Cisco-
           like format.  Specifying either iippvv44 or iippvv66 would extract only
           IPv4 or IPv6 flows respectively.  It has optional parameter
           vveerrbboossee, which is analog of the “show ip cache verbose flow” com‐
           mand. Additionally, hhuummaann parameter can be specify to show selected
           flows in human-readable format.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The fflloowwccttll utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

